  "created": "2026-08-10T09:00:00Z",
  "modified": "2026-08-10T09:00:00Z",
  "language": "en",
  "description": "A document that declares its own fixed sheet geometry and its own @page rule. FRWD is not page-based; this document has simply chosen to be, and the editor must preserve that faithfully rather than reinterpret it."
}
</script>
<style id="frwd-document-style">
@page { size: A4; margin: 12mm; }
:root { color-scheme: light dark; --ink: #14171c; --paper: #fff; }
body { margin: 0; background: #6b6f76; color: var(--ink); font: 400 11pt/1.5 ui-serif, Georgia, serif; }
main { display: block; padding: 8mm; }
.sheet {
  width: 210mm;
  min-height: 297mm;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 18mm;
  background: var(--paper);
  box-shadow: 0 1px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
h1 { font: 600 20pt/1.15 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 4mm; }
p { margin: 0 0 3mm; }
@media print {
  body { background: #fff; }
  main { padding: 0; }
  .sheet { width: auto; min-height: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; box-shadow: none; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main data-frwd-document="">
<article data-frwd-id="f4e3d2c1-0b9a-4867-8564-3d2c1b0a9001" class="sheet">
<h1 data-frwd-id="f4e3d2c1-0b9a-4867-8564-3d2c1b0a9002">Sheet-geometry document</h1>
<p data-frwd-id="f4e3d2c1-0b9a-4867-8564-3d2c1b0a9003">This document declares its own fixed geometry: a 210mm by 297mm sheet, and an <code>@page</code> rule to match. That is document CSS, deliberately authored, and the editor preserves it exactly.</p>
<p data-frwd-id="f4e3d2c1-0b9a-4867-8564-3d2c1b0a9004">It is not evidence that FRWD is page-based. A document may choose to look like paper; the format does not require it, and the editor's own paper view is a separate thing that surrounds the document rather than redefining it.</p>
</article>
</main>

</body></html>